<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<!-- Raises the Fast DDS shared-memory segment and the UDP socket buffers so that a
     camera frame fits in one piece. Sim-only: the ros_gz image bridge does not exist
     on the real aircraft.

     WHY, measured 2026-08-24 (docs/package-status.md 4):
     The ros_gz bridge delivers a fixed FRACTION of each image stream, and that
     fraction collapses at a size boundary:

         down  320x240 RGB8    230 400 B    97% delivered, 0 frames lost
         depth 320x240 F32     307 200 B    97% delivered, 0 frames lost
         down  640x480 RGB8    921 600 B    31-53%
         depth 640x480 F32   1 228 800 B    25-30%

     Every fastrtps segment in /dev/shm measured exactly 549 408 B -- the stock default.
     Both delivered streams fit inside it; both starved streams do not. A sample that
     does not fit falls back to UDP, fragments into 14-19 datagrams against a 208 KB
     default socket buffer (net.core.rmem_default), and losing one fragment loses the
     whole frame. That is the entire mechanism, and it is a TRANSPORT limit -- not a
     sensor limit, not bandwidth, not the frame rate.

     Consequence that made this urgent: front/depth_image feeds obstacle avoidance and
     was delivering 4.8 of 15.6 Hz with a 1256 ms worst-case gap. Reducing its
     resolution WOULD fix delivery but fails the obstacle accuracy gate (a 1.000x0.600 m
     box measures 0.578x0.298 m). This file fixes the transport instead, so no sensor
     is degraded at all.

     🔴 DELIBERATELY NOT SHM-ONLY. config/fastdds_shm_only.xml is a measured dead end
     that severed every /fmu/out/* topic: the PX4 agent links Fast DDS 2.12.2 and ROS
     Humble links 2.6.11, and their SHM segment layouts do not interoperate while
     RTPS-over-UDP does. Both transports are declared here on purpose so that pair can
     still fall back to UDP. Any edit that removes udp_large repeats that failure.

     Sizing: 16 MiB holds five 1.172 MiB depth frames (the SensorDataQoS KEEP_LAST
     depth) plus both RGB streams' histories. /dev/shm has 12 GB and roughly 30 live
     participants, so about 480 MB worst case. -->
<dds xmlns="http://www.eprosima.com/XMLSchemas/fastRTPS_Profiles">
  <profiles>
    <transport_descriptors>
      <transport_descriptor>
        <transport_id>shm_large</transport_id>
        <type>SHM</type>
        <segment_size>16777216</segment_size>
        <port_queue_capacity>4096</port_queue_capacity>
      </transport_descriptor>

      <transport_descriptor>
        <transport_id>udp_large</transport_id>
        <type>UDPv4</type>
        <sendBufferSize>4194304</sendBufferSize>
        <receiveBufferSize>4194304</receiveBufferSize>
      </transport_descriptor>
    </transport_descriptors>

    <participant profile_name="large_samples" is_default_profile="true">
      <rtps>
        <userTransports>
          <transport_id>shm_large</transport_id>
          <transport_id>udp_large</transport_id>
        </userTransports>
        <useBuiltinTransports>false</useBuiltinTransports>
      </rtps>
    </participant>
  </profiles>
</dds>
